1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:06,270
The Strategies list has the built-in strategies. Ones you add appear under My Strategies.

2
00:00:06,370 --> 00:00:10,470
Type in the search box to find one.

3
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:15,910
Click the star to mark a favourite.

4
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:20,370
Right-click a strategy for more: run, test, edit, rename, clone or delete.

5
00:00:20,470 --> 00:00:24,030
Import adds a strategy file that you were sent.

6
00:00:24,130 --> 00:00:29,720
To write your own, start from a copy. Right-click a strategy and choose Clone.

7
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:33,080
The copy appears under My Strategies, and you can change it.

8
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:39,970
Click Edit to open it in the editor.

9
00:00:40,070 --> 00:00:50,960
Click Compile to check it. No errors means it is ready.

10
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:58,480
A mistake is listed with its line. Click it to jump there and fix it.

11
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:03,390
Once it compiles, click Add to save it to your library.

12
00:01:03,490 --> 00:01:08,720
Your strategy is now under My Strategies.

13
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:17,550
Now let's run one and look at it while it works.

14
00:01:17,650 --> 00:01:22,960
The panel on the right shows what it is doing, starting with its log.

15
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:26,630
Stats shows its trades, profit and how long it has run.

16
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:31,840
Edit Vars changes its settings while it runs.

17
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:38,720
Pause stops it trading for a while. Resume starts it again.

18
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:48,930
Stop ends it. Tick the boxes to close its trades and cancel its orders.

